# Main agent orchestration (pointer)

This rule is a pointer only. The single source of truth for main-agent /
worker orchestration, worker language rules, coding-model routing, and
background-worker monitoring is:

`~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/SKILL.md`

Read that file before delegating work, checking worker status, summarizing
workers, or choosing a model/transport for a worker.

Harness notes (do not fork policy here):

- Codex and Claude Code read the same SoT via `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` /
  `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`.
- Sections marked **Cursor-only** in the SoT apply only when this Cursor chat
  is the main agent. Other harnesses ignore those sections.
- Cursor-only Opus workers: `claude-human-stream` in a background Shell.
  Grok land / Grok author: `agent-human-stream --backend grok` (same Shell
  recipe — not Cursor `Task`). Monitor via completion notification.
  See SoT § "Opus transport" + § "Grok transport".
- **Chase work loop (always apply on user install):**
  `~/.cursor/rules/sume-chase-work-loop.mdc`
  (discuss → lock → mega-issue → Opus through MQ enqueue → Grok land).
  SoT § "Chase work loop — discuss → lock → mega-issue → Opus → Grok".
- **Opus Shell cookbook (always apply on user install):**
  `~/.cursor/rules/opus-background-terminal.mdc`
  (`block_until_ms: 0`, prompt file, `cd` not `--cwd`, `--resume`, no Task;
  **default:** Opus fresh-clone → `gt submit` → **`gt` Ready to merge** →
  `gt merge` → STOP, then Grok land babysit; see SoT Graphite hard lock +
  “Review CI ready-signal”).
- **Graphite CI ready-signal (always apply on user install):**
  `~/.cursor/rules/graphite-ci-ready.mdc`
  (`gt info`/`gt log` Ready — not `gh pr checks` loops).
- **Graphite MQ enqueue playbook (always apply on user install):**
  `~/.agents/skills/sume-gt-mq/SKILL.md` — required before any
  `gt submit` / `gt merge` / MQ unstick / land handoff.
- **Active workers Canvas (always apply on user install):**
  `~/.cursor/rules/active-workers-canvas.mdc`
  (maintain `canvases/active-workers-board.canvas.tsx` on launch /
  completion / steer; reconcile terminals ∩ live processes).
- **End-of-turn worker brief (always apply on user install):**
  `~/.cursor/rules/end-of-turn-worker-brief.mdc`
  (every turn: desk + Cursor Cloud worker tables; operating Cloud
  agents are never omitted).
- **Read SoT is `origin/main` (always apply on user install):**
  `~/.cursor/rules/origin-main-sot.mdc`
  (questions about shipped code → `origin/main`, not dirty local main).
- **Worker reasoning effort (always apply on user install):**
  `~/.cursor/rules/worker-reasoning-effort.mdc`
  (code: opus medium / fable high / grok xhigh; research: grok medium,
  opus+fable low).

Re-install the pointer with
`~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/install-cursor-rule.sh --user`
and/or pass repo paths. Edit the SoT skill for policy; keep
`sume-chase-work-loop.mdc`, `opus-background-terminal.mdc`,
`graphite-ci-ready.mdc`, `active-workers-canvas.mdc`, and
`end-of-turn-worker-brief.mdc` in sync when the
loop, Shell recipe, Graphite ready-signal, board, or end-of-turn
brief policy changes.
Enqueue/land ops SoT: `~/.agents/skills/sume-gt-mq/SKILL.md`
(`install-symlinks.sh` in that skill dir).
